ures Democrat Hannah Pingree against Republican Robert Charles, with independent Rick Bennett also on the ballot in a state that no longer uses ranked-choice counting for this contest. Pingree has out-raised Charles roughly two to one and holds a steady polling lead of about ten points, with recent surveys from Siena, UNH, YouGov and Suffolk all showing her ahead by 9 to 14 points. One late Marist likely-voter poll showed a tie, but it stands alone against the broader polling record.\n\nExpert raters overwhelmingly call the race Solid or Likely Democratic, and prediction markets price Pingree at about 96 to 97 percent. Bennett's presence appears to draw more support away from the Republican side, and the Democratic-leaning fundamentals of the state add to Pingree's edge. The race is rated Safe Democratic, with the main uncertainty being the size of the margin rather than the winner.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9757, "margin": 10.9}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9716, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9705, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9685, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9649, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9585, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.96, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9621, "margin": 10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.961, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9719, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9653, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9728, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9678, "margin": 10.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9699, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9727, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.971, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.977, "margin": 11.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9808, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.9762, "margin": 11.5}, {"date": "20